 "figures": {
  "cross": {
   "title": "The brains of one rate against another's",
   "caption": "Each column is a pair of rates of change, written lower\u2013higher; each dot one seed: the share of a world the brains of iteration 1,500 of the higher rate held against those of the lower, the mean of two contests, one in each rate's world. The bar is the median seed; the dashed lines the band of the thesis.",
   "recipe": "**Runs.** The 50 runs of Experiment 9 \u2014 B2 at 10,000 tokens, seeds 1 to 10, with the probability that a brain changes when it is copied at 0.05, 0.1, 0.2 (B2 itself, `B2-10000-s001` \u2026 `-s010`, shared with Experiment 16), 0.4 and 0.8, run to iteration 1,500 at least with a whole world archived every 100. They are made with `python3 gol_lab.py run E09`; every setting is listed in the box under the thesis.\n\n**Data.** From each run's archive, `GraphOfLifeRuns/<run>/archive/world_<iteration>.npz`, kept every 100 iterations.\n\n1. For each seed and each pair of rates, take the worlds of both rates at iteration 1,500. Play two contests, one in each of the two worlds: every agent gets a brain drawn at random from the agents of one rate's world or of the other's, a coin each, mutation is switched off, and 20 iterations are played (`gol_tournament.contest`, brains from two runs).\n2. The higher rate's score is its share of the agents at the end, averaged over the two.\n\n**To make it again:** `python3 book_figures.py rates`."
  },
  "steps": {
   "title": "Each era against the one before, at five rates of change",
   "caption": "One dot per world: the later era's share of the agents, the mean of its two contests with the era before, one in each era's world. The bars are the medians of each rate's ten worlds.",
   "recipe": "**Runs.** The 50 runs of Experiment 9 \u2014 B2 at 10,000 tokens, seeds 1 to 10, with the probability that a brain changes when it is copied at 0.05, 0.1, 0.2 (B2 itself, `B2-10000-s001` \u2026 `-s010`, shared with Experiment 16), 0.4 and 0.8, run to iteration 1,500 at least with a whole world archived every 100. They are made with `python3 gol_lab.py run E09`; every setting is listed in the box under the thesis.\n\n**Data.** From each run's archive, `GraphOfLifeRuns/<run>/archive/world_<iteration>.npz`, kept every 100 iterations.\n\n1. For each world, play each of the eras 0, 100, 200, 500, 1,000 and 1,500 against the one before it, once in each era's world (`gol_tournament.play` with `against=\"previous\"`, 20 iterations, a coin per agent), and average each pair's two shares.\n\n**To make it again:** `python3 book_figures.py rates`."
